{"id": "EUVD-2026-104685", "enisaUuid": "408b183f-1a8c-35a9-872a-e0d8e3236048", "description": "Langchain-Chatchat through 0.3.1.3 exposes a POST /tools/call API endpoint that invokes any registered tool by name without authentication, leaving the always-registered shell tool callable. Remote attackers can send a single request naming the shell tool to execute arbitrary OS commands as the server user (root in the shipped Docker image).", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T00:46:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T14:34:07", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.lasso.security/vulnerability-database/cve-2026-75128", "https://github.com/chatchat-space/Langchain-Chatchat/blob/a6a9193b5002061719f0eee62c6310bd5b1b7f63/libs/chatchat-server/chatchat/server/api_server/tool_routes.py#L33", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/langchain-chatchat-through-0.3.1.3-unauthenticated-rce-via-tools-call-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-75128", "GHSA-5rx2-xp53-9x5r"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "aed880e3-495f-304d-a850-ef76ab7b903e", "product": {"name": "Langchain-Chatchat", "vendor": {"name": "chatchat-space"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.3.1.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b4224cfd-f44b-39c2-b652-699c8acfef85", "vendor": {"name": "chatchat-space"}}], "isExploited": false}